Based on the analysis of component interactions in the system, the following matrix represents the interactions between each component. Each cell (i,j) indicates whether component i interacts with component j:

```
          H   M   C   G   B   T   S
    H  [1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1]
    M  [1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 1, 1]
    C  [1, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 1]
    G  [1, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 1]
    B  [1, 1, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0]
    T  [1, 1, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0]
    S  [1, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 1]
```

Where:
- H = Housing
- M = Motor
- C = Clip
- G = Gear
- B = Battery
- T = Trigger/switch
- S = Shaft

This matrix captures the direct interactions between each component based on their functional and physical connections.
